The chrome uses CSS variables with no default CSS — I need site CSS that styles `.umb-block-grid` (grid display using the vars). Tailwind's site.css won't include that by default. I'll add grid chrome styles in the layout `<style>` or better — include small CSS in the _Layout for umb-block-grid (that's page-level styling, not block component styling; the AGENTS allows editing local blockgrid partials, but CSS is fine in layout). Hmm — cleaner: put the umb-block-grid CSS into the Frontend's site.css? The Frontend src is Vue-focused. Simplest, self-contained: a small `<style>` block in _Layout defining the grid vars. That keeps Tailwind for components. But Tailwind scans views for classes — fine.

Actually better idea: since each block adapter renders a ViewComponent with Tailwind classes, and blocks are columnSpan 12, the umb-block-grid wrapper just needs:
```css
.umb-block-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--umb-block-grid--grid-columns), minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0; }
.umb-block-grid__layout-item { grid-column: span var(--umb-block-grid--item-column-span, 12) / span var(--umb-block-grid--item-column-span, 12); }
```
I'll put that in _Layout <style>.

